-- title:
--   Eigenform ideal in J₀(M) from a maximal Hecke ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $M \geq 1$, let $p$ be a prime, let $S$ be a set of natural numbers, $Q$ a predicate on natural numbers and $c \colon \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{Z}$ a function. Write $\mathbb{T}_2(M)^S$ for [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(M))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid M$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators $U_q$ for primes $q \mid M$ with $q \notin S$. Assume given a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}_2$ of $\mathbb{T}_2(M)^S$ containing the image of $p$ and such that $T_\ell - c(\ell) \in \mathfrak{m}_2$ for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid M$ and $Q(\ell)$. Then, for the degree-zero divisor class group $J_0(M) =$ [`ModularCurve.JZero M`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L115) of the modular function field of level $M$ base changed to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, regarded as a module over the free commutative Hecke algebra $\mathbb{T} = \mathbb{Z}[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ (the polynomial ring [`ModularCurve.HeckeAlg`](def/HeckeGalois_EichlerShimura.html#L14) in indeterminates indexed by the primes) via the action [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleBar M`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeModule.html#L82) by Hecke correspondences, there exists a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$ of $\mathbb{T}$ with the following four properties. First, $\mathfrak{m}$ is an eigenform ideal of level $M$: there are a weight-two cusp form $f$ on $\Gamma_0(M)$ whose $q$-coefficients satisfy $a_1(f) = 1$, multiplicativity at coprime indices, and the recursions $a_{q^{r+2}} = a_q a_{q^{r+1}} - q\,a_{q^r}$ for primes $q \nmid M$ and $a_{q^{r+2}} = a_q a_{q^{r+1}}$ for primes $q \mid M$, a finite field $k$, a subring $\mathcal{O} \subseteq \mathbb{C}$ containing $a_\ell(f)$ for every prime $\ell$, and a ring homomorphism $\varphi \colon \mathcal{O} \to k$, such that $\mathfrak{m}$ is the kernel of the $\mathbb{Z}$-algebra homomorphism $\mathbb{T} \to k$ sending $X_\ell \mapsto \varphi(a_\ell(f))$. Second, $p \in \mathfrak{m}$. Third, $X_\ell - c(\ell) \in \mathfrak{m}$ for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid M$ and $Q(\ell)$. Fourth, the $\mathfrak{m}$-torsion $J_0(M)[\mathfrak{m}]$, the submodule of elements annihilated by every element of $\mathfrak{m}$, is nonzero.
--
--   This is the existence half of the Eichler–Shimura dictionary in weight two: a maximal ideal of the Hecke algebra acting on cusp forms of level $M$ is realised by a normalised eigenform whose associated eigenform ideal, with the prescribed residual Hecke eigenvalues $c(\ell)$ and residue characteristic $p$, has nonvanishing torsion in the Jacobian. It feeds the construction of the family of realisations used in the Mazur-principle and level-lowering steps, being cited by [`ModularCurve.mazurRealizationFamily_of_modRepIsIrreducible_of_isUnramifiedAt`](thm.html#ModularCurve.mazurRealizationFamily_of_modRepIsIrreducible_of_isUnramifiedAt).
